Subject: [PATCH 05/11] feat(pqc-m5): device-identity store speaks the wrap
 envelope
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PQC migration (whitepaper 2.2.2 + 2.2.3 + 2.2.4): device-identity-store
now writes the ML-DSA-65 secret through the AES-256-GCM wrap envelope
(M4) when a SyncWrappingKeyProvider is supplied, and unwraps the
envelope on read. Plaintext and wrapped forms are mutually exclusive in
a single row.

- src/infra/device-identity-store.ts:
  - StoredDeviceIdentity gains 4 nullable mldsa_* fields (public key, plaintext
    private key, wrap envelope BLOB, keyId). Public key read priority:
    mldsa_public_key_pem (M3+) > legacy public_key_pem. Private key:
    wrap envelope is unwrapped via the keyring; otherwise the M1/M2
    plaintext PEM (mldsa_private_key_pem > private_key_pem) is used.
  - generateStoredDeviceIdentity now takes an options object with an
    optional wrappingKeyProvider. When set the secret is wrapped under
    the provider's active key, the wrap envelope is stored in
    mldsa_private_key_wrapped, and mldsa_private_key_pem is left null
    (mutual exclusion).
  - readStoredDeviceIdentity / readStoredDeviceIdentityReadOnly /
    insertStoredDeviceIdentityIfAbsent / repairInvalidStoredDeviceIdentity
    all accept a SyncWrappingKeyProvider through DeviceIdentityReadOptions.
    Wrapped rows are fail-closed: a row read without the keyring that
    sealed it throws, never falling back to the legacy plaintext column.
  - validateStoredDeviceIdentity accepts either a plaintext row (round-trip
    sign/verify) or a wrapped row (envelope fields present, caller may
    have already unwrapped — verified by sign/verify on privateKeyPem).
  - BLOB encoding matches the whitepaper 3.2 contract:
    new TextEncoder().encode(serializeWrappedSecret(wrapped)) — UTF-8
    bytes of a base64url-encoded JSON document, NOT raw JSON.
- src/state/openclaw-state-schema.generated.ts: regenerated-style 4-column
  block mirrored on the generated TS so executeCanonicalStateSchema ships
  the new columns on fresh creates. (openclaw-state-schema.sql carries
  the same 4 lines as the source of truth for any future regeneration.)
- src/infra/device-identity-store.wrap.test.ts: 11 invariants — round-trip
  with keyring, fail-closed no-keyring (read + read-only), dropped keyId
  rejection, BLOB tampered rejection, BLOB shape (UTF-8 base64url JSON),
  plaintext legacy fallback, public-key deviceId stability, two-keyring
  cross-read fails, salvage preserves the wrap envelope, mutual
  exclusion in a single row.

26/26 device-identity-store + 11/11 wrap + 25/25 secret-wrapping +
4/4 schema-additive + 17/17 device-identity + 4 Ed25519-legacy skip
= 79 invariants green across the M2-M5 PQC core.

